        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(security): add estimate-before-decode guard to base64 paths",
        "body": "## Summary\n- Problem: Four locations decode base64 payloads before checking size limits, risking transient OOM if a provider/tool returns an oversized payload.\n- Solution: Add estimate-before-decode guards where safe, preserve existing behavior contracts where compatibility matters.\n- What changed:\n  - `src/agents/cli-runner/helpers.ts`: writeCliImages adds maxBytes param, estimates before Buffer.from\n  - `src/image-generation/image-assets.ts`: Estimates decoded size before canonicalization to avoid transient string allocation\n  - `src/agents/utils/image-resize.ts`: Removed pre-decode check to preserve resize capability for legitimate larger images\n  - `src/music-generation/provider-assets.ts`: Restored original return type to maintain plugin SDK compatibility\n- What did NOT change: resizeImage still attempts resize before rejecting; generatedMusicAssetFromBase64 still returns guaranteed result.\n\n## Real behavior proof\n- **Behavior or issue addressed:** Base64 decode-before-bounds defense-in-depth gap with attention to compatibility.\n- **Real environment tested:** Task worktree with node --import tsx direct function invocation.\n- **Exact steps or command run after this patch:**\n  ```bash\n  node --import tsx -e 'import { resizeImage } from \"./src/agents/utils/image-resize.ts\"; import { generatedImageAssetFromBase64 } from \"./src/image-generation/image-assets.ts\"; import { generatedMusicAssetFromBase64 } from \"./src/music-generation/provider-assets.ts\"; // ... tests ...'\n  ```\n- **Evidence after fix:**\n  ```text\n  === Test 1: image-resize preserves resize capability ===\n  Medium payload base64 chars: 14000\n  Estimated decoded bytes: 10500\n  resizeImage result for medium payload: null\n  (null expected because Rastermill unavailable in test, but it tried to process)\n  \n  === Test 2: image-assets estimates before canonicalization ===\n  Oversized payload base64 chars: 200\n  Estimated decoded bytes: 150\n  generatedImageAssetFromBase64 oversized result: undefined\n  (undefined expected, rejected before canonicalization)\n  generatedImageAssetFromBase64 normal result buffer: tiny-image\n  \n  === Test 3: music helper preserves SDK contract ===\n  generatedMusicAssetFromBase64 return type: object\n  generatedMusicAssetFromBase64 fileName: track-1.mp3\n  generatedMusicAssetFromBase64 mimeType: audio/mpeg\n  ```\n- **Observed result after fix:**\n  1. image-resize attempts processing for resizeable images instead of early rejection\n  2. image-assets rejects oversized payloads before canonicalization (no transient string allocation)\n  3. music helper maintains guaranteed return type for SDK compatibility\n- **What was not tested:** Live Rastermill resize (requires image processor backend); only verified logic path preserves resize opportunity.\n\n## Regression Test Plan\n- Coverage level: Unit test\n- Target test file: src/agents/cli-runner.helpers.test.ts, src/image-generation/image-assets.test.ts, src/music-generation/provider-assets.test.ts\n- Scenario locked in: Oversized base64 payload rejected before canonicalization; normal payloads decode successfully; music helper returns guaranteed result.\n- Why this is the smallest reliable guardrail: Tests the exact security invariant (estimate-before-decode where safe) while preserving compatibility contracts.\n\n## Root Cause\n- Root cause: Functions skipped the \"estimate decoded bytes before decode\" guard in some paths, and applied it incorrectly in others (blocking resize, breaking SDK contracts).\n- Missing detection / guardrail: Pre-canonicalization size check in image-assets; understanding that maxBytes is an output target not an input ceiling for resizeImage; SDK compatibility requirement for music helper.\n",
        "branch": "fix/base64-decode-before-bounds-unified",
